\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 Prologus\~: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat18 [C]lemens papa cuius rem nominis }}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 atque uite subiecti sentiant et tu a domino consequaris zelum scribentis hoc opus deuotum tuo nomini benignus assume \u8230 \'85 et efficacius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 visa animos mouent\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .- (19\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Text: (Am Rande:) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Primus liber continet 30 propositiones\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . Liber I: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat18 [Q]vitquit est causa cause est causa causati}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 . Sic enim causatum a cuius causa b sit, c autem sit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 causa \u8230 \'85 vnde a primo trinitas illa est unitas deitatis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .- (21\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Liber II: [B]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 onum est quod\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 utiliter habet esse \u8230 \'85 male merens magna puniendus est pena\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .- (23\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Liber III\~: [H]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 omo lapsus et penitens debet diuina misericordia subleuari. Cum ex fragilitate propria sit homo in lubrico\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 constitutus \u8230 \'85 nisi fuerit diuino remedio reparatus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .- (24\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Liber IV\~: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Predicatio est oratio ad salutem persuadens anime. Sacramentum est res uisibilis \u8230 \'85 ergo non est digna ablutione peccati\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .- (25\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Liber V: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Resurrectio est anime et corporis morte separatorum iterata coniunctio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Vtrum  enim bene et male merendo laborat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 (25\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Tormento perpetuo dampnatorum nulla maior est pena. Quod enim dampnatorum maius quam deum amittere \u8230 \'85 et sic patet\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 propositum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . - Gegen\u252 \'fcber PL hat diese Hs. noch eine Fortsetzung (25\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -17\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ): >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Incipiunt maxime\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 speciales theologie de attributis iudicis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 < (am Rande angemerkt). [P]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 otentia est vis facilis aliquem motum operari. Scientia est uis apprehensiua causarum per quas et propter quas aliquid\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 habet esse\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 Endet (27\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 )\~: [P]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ater omne iudicium dedit filio ipse nichilominus et spiritus sanctus. Coniudicabunt. Pater dicitur dedisse filio \u8230 \'85 qui apparebit hominibus iudicandis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 homo iudex. -\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   PL 210, 595 A \endash  618 B [ohne die Fortsetzung). - 28\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  leer.
\par \pard\sl360\slmult1\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \par}

