\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 150\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -151\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24    {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6922/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat18 Collectio auctoritatum de conversione Pauli apostoli}}
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat18 Saulus aduc (!) inspirans minarum et cedis in discipulos domini (Act 9,1). Si secundum sentenciam saluatoris luce 15: Gaudium est super uno peccatore penitentia agente (Lc 15,7)}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quanto magis de penitente, qui non solum penitet, sed patet totum mundum ad penitentiam provocat, verum vnde verba hortans premissa omnibus super \u8250 \'9bBeati immaculati\u8249 \'8b\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Ps 118,1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 dicit: Merito gaudent angeli de conuersione peccatorum, quia is, qui erravit, iam non errat, iam oblitus est suum errorem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Ambrosius Mediolanensis, Expositio in psalmum David, sermo 22, ed. PL 15, 1512A) ... \endash  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quia non putabat ihesum in celo esse, sed magis dampnatum tamquam falsum prophetam dixit propter vocem, que fuit cum stupore: Dicerem, que me vix faterer\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  151a\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -151b\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  leer.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Sammlung von Kirchenv\u228 \'e4ter-Zitaten zur Bekehrung des Apostels Paulus; nachweisbar sind u. a.: Ps.-Ambrosius Mediolanensis, De sancta Quadragesima, sermo 23, ed. PL 17, 650AB. \endash  Ps.-Aurelius Augustinus, sermo 189: In festo Conversionis sancti Pauli, ed. PL 39, 2098. \endash  Hrabanus Maurus, De vita beatae Mariae Magdalenae et sorroris eius sanctae Marthae, c. 36, ed. PL 112, 1490D. \endash  Aurelius Augustinus, De spiritu et littera, c. 7, ed. PL 44, 207.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \par}

