\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 1. 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -85\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vc\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24    {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Liber Leviticus cum Glossa ordinaria}}
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Prothemata: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Esicius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 <\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 . {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Si quis querat quare legis libri diuisi sunt}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 , cum historia tempore indiuisa sit. Respondendum est, ut fastidium lectori aufferret diuisio librorum, sicut et uie spatia diuidit uiator, tanquam diuisus labor minuatur labor\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (expungiert). \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Stegm\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \u252 \'fc\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 ller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , RB, Nr. 11783\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 3\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Esicius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 <\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 . Querendum est quare liber iste leuiticus dicitur, quia scilicet in hoc nomine tocius libri argumentum manifestatur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ... \endash  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 a quibus liber ille congruum sortitus est nomen, quibus hec omnia digerit per ordinem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Stegm\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \u252 \'fc\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 ller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , RB, Nr. 11783\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Isidorus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 <\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 . Omnis historiarum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (expungiert) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 diuersitas christi hostiam prefigurabat. Vnde, ueritate oblata, cessauit umbra, nec sacrificium prefigurans ueri et eterni sacerdotis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ... \endash  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 panes azimos, cum non in fermento malicie, sed in azimis sinceritatis et veritatis epulamur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Stegm\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \u252 \'fc\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 ller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , RB, Nr. 11783\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 7\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -85\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vc\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Glossa marginalis: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Esicius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 <\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 . {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[2].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 \u8250 \'9bVocauit autem moysen\u8249 \'8b. Per coniunctionem autem sequencia iungit precedentibus}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 , inicium, scilicet illius libri fini precedentis .\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .. \endash  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 sed opportunum dispensacioni eorum dispensatur exordium: \u8250 \'9bHec sunt nomina filiorum israel, qui ingressi sunt egyptum\u8249 \'8b\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Ex 1,1). \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Stegm\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \u252 \'fc\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 lle\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , RB, Nr. 11783\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 9\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 \u8250 \'9bEt non redimetur\u8249 \'8b. Discipuli nostri quando fiunt perfecti, nihil nostri egent magisterii \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ... \endash  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 perfecta enim demonstrata sunt, quia intencionem diuinam celestemque gerunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 (2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -85\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Glossa interlinearis: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 \u8250 \'9bVocauit autem moysen\u8249 \'8b. LXX: Reuocauit. Celo uel scriptura, in qua ymagines}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  et figure misteriorum in futurarum rerum testimonium\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ... \endash  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 cuius laus non ex hominibus, sed ex deo est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Stegm\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \u252 \'fc\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 ller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , RB, Nr. 11783\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 14\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 \u8250 \'9bHec sunt precepta\u8249 \'8b. Qui poterat intelligere misteria. Qui infirmi et non capaces misterii.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -85\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Bibeltext: Lv 1,1-27,34. \endash  33\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  leer.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Stegm\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 \u252 \'fc\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 ller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , RB, Nr. 11783. \endash  Druck der Glossa ordinaria: PL 113, 295-380. \endash  Lit.:\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 J. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 de Blic\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , L'\u339 \'9cuvre ex\u233 \'e9g\u233 \'e9tique de Walafrid Strabon et la \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs20 Glossa ordinaria\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , in: \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Recherches de th\u233 \'e9ologie ancienne et m\u233 \'e9di\u233 \'e9vale\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  16 (1949), S. 5-28\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 . \endash  R. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Wiel\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf1 ockx\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 , Autour de la \u171 \'abGlossa ordinaria\u187 \'bb, in: Recherches de th\u233 \'e9ologie ancienne et m\u233 \'e9di\u233 \'e9vale 49 (1982), S. 222-228. \endash  G. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Lobrichon\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 , Une nouveaut\u233 \'e9: les gloses de la Bible, in: Le Moyen Age et la Bible. Hrsg. von P. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Rich\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf1 \u233 \'e9\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 . Paris 1984 (Bible de tous les temps 4), S. 95-114. \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 B. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Smalley\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Glossa ordinaria, in: TRE 13 (1984), S. 452-457. \endash  B. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Smalley\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 The study of the Bible in the Middle Ages. \u179 \'b3Oxford 1984, S. 46-66. \endash  K. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Froehlich\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 , Walahfrid Strabo and the \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Glossa ordinaria\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 : The Making of a Myth, in: Latin Authors (other than Augustine and his Opponents), \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Nachleben\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1  of the Fathers. Papers presented at the Eleventh International Conference on Patristic Studies held in Oxford 1991. Hrsg. von E. A. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Livingstone.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1  L\u246 \'f6wen 1993 (Studia patristica 28), S. 192-196.}

